#section[Professional Experience]

#table(
  columns: (1fr, auto),
  stroke: none,
  inset: 0pt,
  [
    #text(weight: "bold")[Template.net]
    \
    #text(size: 9pt, fill: rgb("#666"))[Full Stack Engineer]
  ],
  [
    #align(right)[12/2020 – Present]
  ],
)

*Template.net* is an AI-powered browser-based content creation platform serving 10M+ users, offering collaborative editors for graphics, documents, and whiteboards.

- Developed and maintained a web-based graphic editor using *React*, *Redux*, and *TypeScript*.
- Implemented a *feature-based architecture* to improve code modularity, maintainability, and extensibility.
- Built scalable frontend architectures using *micro-frontends* and *Module Federation*.
- Developed the homepage with *Next.js*, applying rendering strategies and caching to improve *performance* and *SEO*.
- Optimized frontend rendering, *bundle size*, and overall application performance.
- Developed *scalable and reliable backend services* using *NestJS*, *PostgreSQL*, *MongoDB*, *Redis*, and *Docker*.
- Optimized *API performance* by reducing *response latency* and improving backend efficiency.
- Applied *application security best practices*, including authentication, authorization, input validation, access control, and rate limiting, to protect against common vulnerabilities and secure API endpoints.
- Implemented *real-time collaboration* using *WebSockets* to support multi-user editing.
- Implemented *NestJS microservices* with *message queues* for reliable asynchronous processing.
- Integrated *Redis caching* to improve backend performance and efficiency.
- Built *CI/CD pipelines* using *GitHub Actions*, configured AWS authentication through *OIDC*.
- Collaborated with *cross-functional teams* to deliver end-to-end product features.
- Leveraged *AI-assisted development tools*, including *GitHub Copilot* and *Claude Code*, to accelerate development and improve code quality.

